[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4667585735","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120128#issuecomment-4667585735","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120128","id":4667585735,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABFjW0xw","user":{"login":"lawnjelly","id":21999379,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxOTk5Mzc5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21999379?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly","html_url":"https://github.com/lawnjelly","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-06-10T07:13:23Z","updated_at":"2026-06-10T07:41:05Z","body":"I *think* I agree that the second init is redundant, but would be good to have another pair of eyes on this, as it's a bit \"jumpy aroundy\", and it's some time since I looked at variant.\r\n\r\nIt was introduced here: #43421 . It certainly seems like the intention matches this interpretation.\r\n\r\nThe `is_local` seems to refer to whether the data is locally stored on the `Variant` versus the larger types (`Transform` etc) which are stored in pools.\r\n\r\nIt looks fine for local types but needs checking it works ok with the non-local types. I suspect the local types would have been optimized out anyway so the non-local types might be the big win here.\r\n\r\nRunning out of time to debug here so maybe someone else can step through the non local case (who is more familiar with Variant in 4.x).\r\n\r\n_(Just adding a `return` in the if branch might be an alternative, with a comment to note that the second `init` is not required.)_","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4667585735/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4668091350","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120128#issuecomment-4668091350","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120128","id":4668091350,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABFj1r1g","user":{"login":"aurpine","id":12262539,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMjYyNTM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12262539?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aurpine","html_url":"https://github.com/aurpine","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aurpine/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aurpine/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aurpine/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aurpine/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aurpine/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aurpine/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aurpine/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aurpine/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aurpine/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-06-10T08:21:07Z","updated_at":"2026-06-11T22:36:11Z","body":"<details>\r\n<summary>Old response</summary>\r\nI left it out originally because I wasn't sure, but I tested `Basis` which is one of the non local cases and it initialized the identity matrix properly. Taking another look at the templates, I think I understand now. The five `_VariantInternalAccessorElsewhere` cases (namely `Transform2D`, `Transform3D`, `AABB`, `Projection`, and `Basis`) all have their own specialized template for `VariantInitializer` that call their respective `init_*` function. These all just call `memnew_placement` in the inits. So I think these are also identical.\r\n\r\nThen there's the PackedArray case. In the init, they call something like\r\n```\r\nv->_data.packed_array = Variant::PackedArrayRef<uint8_t>::create(Vector<uint8_t>());\r\n```\r\n`create` is:\r\n```\r\nreturn memnew(PackedArrayRef<T>);\r\n```\r\nNow I don't know if this is the same as the default initializer since it's using memnew instead of placement. \r\n</details>\r\n\r\n-----\r\nBoth the non-local cases (pooled allocation and packed arrays) do allocation differently and then construct an object. The accessors account for this, so the `VariantDefaultInitializer` construction is also redundant. I updated the PR description.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4668091350/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4668178119","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120128#issuecomment-4668178119","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120128","id":4668178119,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABFj6-xw","user":{"login":"aurpine","id":12262539,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMjYyNTM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12262539?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aurpine","html_url":"https://github.com/aurpine","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aurpine/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aurpine/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aurpine/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aurpine/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aurpine/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aurpine/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aurpine/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aurpine/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aurpine/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-06-10T08:32:28Z","updated_at":"2026-06-10T08:32:28Z","body":"Did some preliminary testing on other types (PR editor vs beta 5 editor). I didn't see any difference on `PackedByteArray` and I actually saw slightly worse performance with `Basis`. I will take a deeper look later.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4668178119/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4672663652","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120128#issuecomment-4672663652","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120128","id":4672663652,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABFoMwZA","user":{"login":"aurpine","id":12262539,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMjYyNTM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12262539?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aurpine","html_url":"https://github.com/aurpine","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aurpine/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aurpine/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aurpine/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aurpine/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aurpine/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aurpine/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aurpine/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aurpine/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aurpine/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-06-10T17:24:01Z","updated_at":"2026-06-10T18:40:27Z","body":"With that insight, the issue is now that `VariantInitializer` [default-initializes](https://en.cppreference.com/cpp/language/default_initialization) whereas `VariantDefaultInitializer` [value-initializes](https://en.cppreference.com/cpp/language/value_initialization). \r\n\r\nIn the class case, they both call the default constructor. In the primitive type case, no initialization occurs when default-initialized. Since `VariantDefaultInitializer` is called afterwards, we always overwrite with value initialization. With that in mind, would it suffice to change `VariantInitializer` to do value-initialization instead? \r\n\r\n```diff\r\n- memnew_placement(&VariantInternalAccessor<T>::get(v), T);\r\n+ memnew_placement(&VariantInternalAccessor<T>::get(v), T());\r\n```\r\n\r\nNow the question is whether this change from default to value initialization is ever undesirable where only `VariantInitializer` is used. ~But as you mentioned, `VariantInitializer` calls `clear` which zeroes the memory anyways.~ nvm this doesn't apply to primitives","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4672663652/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4673745780","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120128#issuecomment-4673745780","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120128","id":4673745780,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABFpOzdA","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-06-10T19:33:56Z","updated_at":"2026-06-10T19:34:37Z","body":"> In the class case, they both call the default constructor. In the primitive type case, no initialization occurs when default-initialized. Since VariantDefaultInitializer is called afterwards, we always overwrite with value initialization. With that in mind, would it suffice to change VariantInitializer to do value-initialization instead?\r\n\r\nPerhaps. The trade-off is wasted computation on values, but if the difference truly only affects primitives, it's a better trade-off than setting expensive values twice.\r\n\r\nMy eventual plan was to remove `VariantInitializer` entirely, instead surfacing an init-function from `VariantInternal` instead that uses templates to let callers choose how to initialize. I didn't get around to it yet (and I'm not sure of the best end shape either).","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4673745780/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4674347425","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120128#issuecomment-4674347425","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120128","id":4674347425,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABFpzhoQ","user":{"login":"aurpine","id":12262539,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMjYyNTM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12262539?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aurpine","html_url":"https://github.com/aurpine","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aurpine/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aurpine/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aurpine/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aurpine/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aurpine/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aurpine/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aurpine/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aurpine/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aurpine/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-06-10T20:49:19Z","updated_at":"2026-06-12T05:37:32Z","body":"Oh interesting. I could try going the other direction and skip `VariantInitializer` instead. Though I encountered crashes when trying this out, even when setting the type. Has something to do with `Transform2D`.\r\n\r\nEdit: I think we should prefer the `memnew_placement` of  `VariantInitializer` as it is more optimized.\r\n\r\nMy performance testing setup doesn't hit the codepath for primitive types. GDScript might be optimizing it out somewhere. I am seeing `OPCODE_ASSIGN_NULL` when debugging primitive variant construction.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4674347425/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4737782612","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120128#issuecomment-4737782612","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120128","id":4737782612,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABGmTTVA","user":{"login":"aurpine","id":12262539,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMjYyNTM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12262539?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aurpine","html_url":"https://github.com/aurpine","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aurpine/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aurpine/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aurpine/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aurpine/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aurpine/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aurpine/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aurpine/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aurpine/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aurpine/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-06-18T03:57:31Z","updated_at":"2026-06-18T03:57:31Z","body":"I made the change to `VariantInitializer`, added tests and updated the PR description.\r\n\r\nThe tests fail without the `VariantInitializer` change, so this gives me confidence that we now have parity with `VariantDefaultInitializer`. Specifically, the `bool`, `int` and `float` cases do not zero out the data if only `VariantInitializer` is called. ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4737782612/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4758875130","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120128#issuecomment-4758875130","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120128","id":4758875130,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABG6ar-g","user":{"login":"aurpine","id":12262539,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMjYyNTM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12262539?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aurpine","html_url":"https://github.com/aurpine","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aurpine/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aurpine/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aurpine/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aurpine/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aurpine/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aurpine/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aurpine/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aurpine/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aurpine/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-06-20T15:57:37Z","updated_at":"2026-06-23T01:23:27Z","body":"The unit tests can be made much shorter with the doctest [`GENERATE`](https://github.com/doctest/doctest/blob/master/doc/markdown/parameterized-tests.md) macro added in 2.5.0 (we are on 2.4.11). I opened #120563 to update it. Seeing as this will likely land first, I will follow up afterwards.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4758875130/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4768800511","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120128#issuecomment-4768800511","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120128","id":4768800511,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABHD4e_w","user":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-06-22T13:28:24Z","updated_at":"2026-06-22T17:30:28Z","body":"Needs squash","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4768800511/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":1},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":{"reason":"resolved"}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4778976383","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120128#issuecomment-4778976383","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120128","id":4778976383,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABHNlkfw","user":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-06-23T12:02:31Z","updated_at":"2026-06-23T12:02:31Z","body":"Thanks!","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4778976383/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]